  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nGuidance continues to point towards the subtropical high shifting\neast of the region starting Friday as a troughing pattern develops \nover the Northwest US/along the West Coast. As the trough pushes \neastward, PWATs will begin to improve, reaching near 1.5\"-1.7\" by\nSaturday and lasting through at least the weekend. 1000-700MB \nmixing ratios are forecast to increase to 10-12 g/kg, enough to\nsupport rain chances even over the lower deserts, with NBM/WPC \nPoPs currently reflecting 20-30% chances across South-Central AZ.\nThis is a decent increase from previous runs but still several \ndays out, so models are still subject to change. Temperatures \nare forecast to drop closer to late August normals by Sunday or \nearly next week as falling midlevel heights and an increase in \nmoisture/cloud cover over the eastern CWA support a cooling trend \n(more pronounced across South-Central AZ).",
